From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 20:58:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: dt: allow an idle state to be disabled by default

Map a new "idle-state-disabled-by-default" boolean onto
CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF, so a DT platform can register a state that neither
the governors nor the s2idle path will use until userspace explicitly
clears its per-CPU "disable" attribute.

This is for states that are only safe inside system suspend.  On
msm8998 the system-level power collapse state stops the XO, which stops
the QTIMER: entered from normal idle, the next timer expiry is simply
never delivered and the machine sleeps through every alarm.  Entered
from s2idle -- after a sleep hook enables it -- wakeup comes from
hardware MPM pins and the state is sound.  CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF is the
existing in-kernel mechanism for exactly this "registered but opt-in"
semantic (registration ORs it into states_usage[].disable as
CPUIDLE_STATE_DISABLED_BY_USER); it only lacked a DT spelling.

Both selection paths honour the disable bit: find_deepest_state()
skips disabled states for s2idle, and the governors skip them for
normal idle, so an enable/disable pair around suspend gives a clean
"s2idle only" gate with no new cpuidle mechanism.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_states.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_states.c b/drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_states.c
index 558d49838990..f9853f31ff1c 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_states.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_states.c
@@ -79,6 +79,8 @@ static int init_state_node(struct cpuidle_state *idle_state,
 	idle_state->flags = CPUIDLE_FLAG_RCU_IDLE;
 	if (of_property_read_bool(state_node, "local-timer-stop"))
 		idle_state->flags |= CPUIDLE_FLAG_TIMER_STOP;
+	if (of_property_read_bool(state_node, "idle-state-disabled-by-default"))
+		idle_state->flags |= CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF;
 	/*
 	 * TODO:
 	 *	replace with kstrdup and pointer assignment when name
